<!-- ================= WHO IT ISN'T FOR ================= -->
<section class="band band--ink">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="col">
      <p class="eyebrow rise">Read this before you order</p>
      <h2 class="wide rise">This stool asks you to kneel. For some people that rules it out.</h2>
      <p class="rise">To use it you have to get down onto your knees, fold your shins under, and get back up afterwards.</p>
      <p class="rise"><strong style="color:#fff">If you can't get down to the floor at all, this is the wrong product.</strong> If your knee won't bend far enough to kneel, or if rising from the floor is the movement you can no longer make, a stool will not solve that and we're not going to tell you it will. What you want is a proper prayer chair, and there are several sold in the UK. Buy one of those.</p>
      <p class="rise">This is for the person who can still get down and can still make sujud — but can't hold the sitting in between. If that's you, we don't know of anything else built for it.</p>
      <p class="rise" style="margin-bottom:0">We'd rather lose the order than have it arrive and be wrong for you.</p>
